# Session-Summary-Check - the closing "what shipped / what is left" report.
#
# Copy to .env next to this file and edit. One setting, and its default is the
# result of getting this wrong twice in both directions - see below. The one
# knob deliberately NOT offered is an enable/disable flag:
#
# COOLDOWN_MINUTES - minutes before the requirement is delivered again in the
# same session. Default 15.
#
# This exists because BOTH extremes failed in practice. With no cooldown the
# hook asked on every Stop, so each time another gate blocked, the agent
# rewrote the whole summary - four copies in one turn. Latching it to once per
# session then went too far the other way: the requirement landed on the first
# Stop, which in a long session is an intermediate one, and the turn that
# actually ended the work carried no reminder at all.
#
# A window collapses the burst (blocked Stops arrive seconds apart) while
# still re-arming before a long session ends. 0 means deliver on every Stop -
# that is the looping behaviour, so do not set it without a reason.
COOLDOWN_MINUTES=15

#   * NO ENABLE/DISABLE FLAG. A summary that can be switched off per project
#     is a summary the next session cannot rely on having. Remove the hook if
#     it is genuinely unwanted; do not leave it installed and mute.
#
# The hook reads no project content and writes nothing outside Hook Maker's
# own state directory. It never blocks: a gate that blocks sends the agent
# back to work, and anything it does then lands after the summary, which is
# precisely what this hook is supposed to prevent.
